+# Epic Breakdown: Pulseboard
+
+**Project**: Pulseboard  
+**Date**: 2026-08-11  
+**Total Epics**: 3 (E000 plus 2 product epics)  
+**Estimated Total Stories**: 11–16
+
+---
+
+## Epic Dependency Map
+
+```text
+E000 Developer Infrastructure
+  |
+  +--> E001 Reviewed Workspace Action Capture
+         |
+         +--> E002 Confirmed Reminder Delivery
+```
+
+## Epic Prioritization
+
+### MVP Epics
+
+- E000: Developer Infrastructure
+- E001: Reviewed Workspace Action Capture
+- E002: Confirmed Reminder Delivery
+
+No enhancement or future epics are planned in this four-week pilot corpus. The plan deliberately stays below the Build four-epic complexity gate.
+
+---
+
+## Epic Definitions
+
+### E000: Developer Infrastructure
+
+**Value Statement**: Establish a reliable and observable delivery baseline so the pilot loop can be built and checked safely.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Configure a single local command for relevant checks, automated CI checks, environment/configuration conventions, and pilot-appropriate error visibility. This is included because the project is production-bound enough to deliver reminders and handle workspace-scoped data.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] Relevant tests and checks run locally with a documented command.
+- [ ] CI runs lint, tests, and build checks for changes.
+- [ ] Configuration distinguishes local and deployed environments without exposing secrets.
+- [ ] Failures in the pilot path can be observed with useful context.
+
+**User Stories Summary**:
+
+- Testing and test-data patterns for API and browser UI
+- CI, linting, formatting, and build checks
+- Environment configuration and secrets-handling conventions
+- Error visibility for the pilot path
+
+**Dependencies**:
+
+- **Depends On**: None
+- **Enables**: E001, E002
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies)**:
+
+- Migrations: —
+- Models/Services: test configuration and error-reporting integration boundary
+- Files/Components: CI workflow, project tooling configuration, environment templates, test harness
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 3–5  
+**Priority**: P0 — Foundation  
+**Target Phase**: Phase 0
+
+---
+
+### E001: Reviewed Workspace Action Capture
+
+**Value Statement**: Enable meeting facilitators to turn an uploaded transcript into workspace-safe, reviewed action items without losing human control.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Build the browser and Python API flow for transcript upload, action-item proposal extraction, proposal review, and explicit confirmation of action text, owner, and due date. Scope all records and request paths to a workspace so a user cannot read another workspace's transcripts or actions.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] A facilitator can upload a transcript and receive proposed action items.
+- [ ] A facilitator can review and correct a proposal before confirming it.
+- [ ] Scheduling is unavailable until the facilitator explicitly confirms text, owner, and due date.
+- [ ] A real-role negative probe cannot retrieve another workspace's transcripts or actions.
+
+**User Stories Summary**:
+
+- Workspace-scoped transcript upload and storage
+- Proposed action extraction and display
+- Review, correction, and explicit confirmation of text, owner, and due date
+- Workspace authorization and cross-workspace negative-path coverage
+
+**Dependencies**:
+
+- **Depends On**: E000
+- **Enables**: E002
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies)**:
+
+- Migrations: workspace-scoped transcripts, action proposals, confirmed-action state
+- Models/Services: transcript ingestion, proposal extraction, confirmation guard, workspace authorization
+- Files/Components: transcript upload, proposal review, confirmation UI, API routes and request-role enforcement
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 5–7  
+**Priority**: P0 — MVP critical  
+**Target Phase**: Phase 1
+
+---
+
+### E002: Confirmed Reminder Delivery
+
+**Value Statement**: Enable facilitators to dispatch one reminder only for a confirmed action and see whether it was delivered.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Add a configurable reminder-provider adapter, scheduling/dispatch for confirmed actions, and an observable delivery status in the browser UI. The provider is deliberately not selected at planning time; the epic must preserve that configuration seam.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] A confirmed action can schedule and dispatch one reminder through the configured provider.
+- [ ] An unconfirmed or incomplete action cannot be scheduled or dispatched.
+- [ ] The facilitator can view delivery status for the action.
+- [ ] Runtime evidence exercises upload → confirmation → delivery using the configured provider path.
+- [ ] The facilitator LARP finds the control boundary and delivery outcome understandable.
+
+**User Stories Summary**:
+
+- Configurable reminder-provider integration boundary
+- Scheduling and guarded dispatch of confirmed actions
+- Delivery-status persistence and display
+- End-to-end runtime evidence and facilitator LARP preparation
+
+**Dependencies**:
+
+- **Depends On**: E000, E001
+- **Enables**: Pilot measurement and outcome evaluation
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies)**:
+
+- Migrations: reminder schedules and delivery-status records linked to confirmed actions
+- Models/Services: provider adapter, scheduling/dispatch service, delivery-status update path
+- Files/Components: reminder configuration, confirmed-action scheduling control, delivery-status UI, API routes
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 3–4  
+**Priority**: P0 — MVP critical  
+**Target Phase**: Phase 2
+
+---
+
+## Epic Execution Strategy
+
+### Phase 0: Developer Infrastructure
+
+**Goal**: Establish a reliable and observable delivery baseline.
+
+**Epic**: E000
+
+**Success Gate**: Local checks, CI, configuration conventions, and error visibility are operating before feature work.
+
+### Phase 1: Controlled Capture
+
+**Goal**: Give facilitators a workspace-safe way to review and confirm proposed actions.
+
+**Epic**: E001
+
+**Success Gate**: The facilitator can complete upload → review → explicit confirmation, while real-role cross-workspace access is denied.
+
+### Phase 2: Controlled Delivery
+
+**Goal**: Close the loop with guarded reminder dispatch and observable delivery status.
+
+**Epic**: E002
+
+**Success Gate**: Runtime evidence covers upload → confirmation → delivery and a facilitator LARP finds the result understandable.
+
+## Risk Mitigation by Epic
+
+| Epic | Primary Risk | Mitigation Strategy |
+|---|---|---|
+| E000 | Product work lacks a reliable feedback and deployment baseline | Establish checks, CI, configuration, and error visibility first |
+| E001 | Incorrect or cross-workspace actions undermine trust | Explicit confirmation gate plus real-role isolation probe |
+| E002 | Provider uncertainty or failed dispatch is hidden | Configurable adapter and visible delivery status |
+
+## Success Metrics by Epic
+
+| Epic | Key Metric | Target | Measurement |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| E000 | Required checks run automatically | All configured checks pass before merge | CI results |
+| E001 | Proposals reviewed | 80% during pilot | Proposal-created and proposal-reviewed events |
+| E002 | Unowned overdue actions | 30% reduction in four weeks | Baseline versus pilot action-status comparison |
+
+## Notes
+
+- The plan has three total epics, so concurrency waves and wave-safety validation are not required at Build level.
+- E002 is intentionally sequential: it consumes the confirmed, workspace-scoped action state from E001.
+- Exact provider choice and low-level architecture remain reversible story-planning decisions; they must not weaken the explicit confirmation and workspace-isolation promises.
